<% content_for :title, "Privacy" %>

<article class="max-w-2xl">
  <header class="mb-8">
    <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-extrabold tracking-tight">Privacy</h1>
    <p class="mt-3 text-ink-muted">What Purple stores about you, why, and how to have it removed.</p>
  </header>

  <div class="space-y-8 leading-relaxed">
    <section aria-labelledby="who">
      <h2 id="who" class="text-xl font-bold">Who runs Purple</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-ink-muted">
        Purple is run by <strong class="text-ink">Darren Jones</strong>, an individual based in the
        UK, who is the controller of your data under UK data protection law (the UK GDPR and the Data
        Protection Act 2018). Questions and requests go to
        <%= mail_to "privacy@purple.daz.codes", nil, class: "text-purple-team underline" %>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="what">
      <h2 id="what" class="text-xl font-bold">What we store</h2>
      <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-2 pl-6 text-ink-muted">
        <li><strong class="text-ink">Your account:</strong> your email address, your display name and
          your password, which is stored only as a one-way hash that nobody can read back.</li>
        <li><strong class="text-ink">Sign-ins:</strong> for each device you're signed in on, its IP
          address and browser, so you can see and sign out your sessions on your account page.</li>
        <li><strong class="text-ink">Your play:</strong> the moves you make in missions and Workshop
          campaigns, your scores, XP, levels, streaks and badges.</li>
        <li><strong class="text-ink">Server logs:</strong> the IP address, time and page of each
          request, used to keep the site secure and fix faults. Logs are overwritten automatically as
          new ones come in.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="mt-3 text-ink-muted">
        Everything inside the game is fictional. The staff numbers, passwords and other "private
        details" you can share in a mission are made up for your character, and the sign-in pages in
        the game never record what you type. Never enter a real password into a game page.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="why">
      <h2 id="why" class="text-xl font-bold">Why, and on what basis</h2>
      <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-2 pl-6 text-ink-muted">
        <li><strong class="text-ink">To provide the game you signed up for</strong> (contract):
          your account, signing you in, scoring your play, keeping your progress and showing
          leaderboards. We email you only to confirm your address and to reset your password.</li>
        <li><strong class="text-ink">To keep Purple secure and working</strong> (legitimate
          interests): sign-in records, server logs and reports of errors, which never include your
          email address or what you typed.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="mt-3 text-ink-muted">
        There's no advertising, no tracking or analytics, and we don't sell your data or use it for
        anything else.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="public">
      <h2 id="public" class="text-xl font-bold">What other players see</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-ink-muted">
        Your display name, levels, badges and preferred side are on your public profile, and on the
        leaderboards unless you opt out on your account page. Your email address is never shown.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="cookies">
      <h2 id="cookies" class="text-xl font-bold">Cookies</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-ink-muted">
        Two cookies, both needed for the site to work: one keeps you signed in, and one protects
        forms from being submitted by other websites and carries one-off messages like "Signed out".
        There are no tracking cookies, so there's no cookie banner.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="where">
      <h2 id="where" class="text-xl font-bold">Who else handles it</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-ink-muted">
        A few providers handle data on our behalf, only to run Purple:
      </p>
      <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-2 pl-6 text-ink-muted">
        <li><strong class="text-ink">Hetzner</strong> hosts the server and database, in Finland (EU).</li>
        <li><strong class="text-ink">Resend</strong> sends our emails, from its EU region, so it sees
          your email address and the message.</li>
        <li><strong class="text-ink">Cloudflare</strong> stores copies of our database backups
          (R2 storage).</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="mt-3 text-ink-muted">
        Resend and Cloudflare are US companies, so your data may be accessed from the US. Where it
        is, it's protected by the UK's adequacy arrangements for the US or by the standard data
        protection clauses in their contracts.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="how-long">
      <h2 id="how-long" class="text-xl font-bold">How long we keep it</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-ink-muted">
        Your account and play are kept while you have an account. When it's deleted, they're removed
        from the live database straight away and drop out of backups within 30 days. Records of
        devices you've signed out of are removed when you sign out.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="age">
      <h2 id="age" class="text-xl font-bold">Age</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-ink-muted">
        You need to be 13 or over to make an account. If we learn that an account belongs to someone
        younger, we'll delete it.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="rights">
      <h2 id="rights" class="text-xl font-bold">Your rights</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-ink-muted">
        You can ask for a copy of your data, ask us to correct it, object to how we use it, or ask us
        to delete your account and everything linked to it, by emailing
        <%= mail_to "privacy@purple.daz.codes", nil, class: "text-purple-team underline" %>. We'll reply
        within a month. If you're unhappy with how we handle your data, you can complain to the
        Information Commissioner's Office at
        <%= link_to "ico.org.uk", "https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/", class: "text-purple-team underline" %>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted">Last updated 16 November 2026.</p>
  </div>
</article>
